    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s20",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I have learned by experience and can tell you that there are few who have taken of the useful things of Egypt and come out of it,",
    "chunk_index": 36,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s21",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s21",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and have then prepared what is required for the service of God; but Ader the Edomite on the other hand has many a brother.",
    "chunk_index": 37,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s22",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s22",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "I mean those who, founding on some piece of Greek learning, have brought forth heretical ideas, and have as it were made golden calves in Bethel, which is, being interpreted, the house of God.",
    "chunk_index": 38,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s23",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s23",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "This appears to me to be intended to convey that such persons set up their own images in the Scriptures in which the Word of God dwells, and which therefore are tropically called Bethel.",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s24",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s24",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The other image is said in the word to have been set up in Dan.",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s25",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s25",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now the borders of Dan are at the extremities and are contiguous to the country of the heathens, as is plainly recorded in the Book of Jesus, son of Nave.",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
      235,
      240
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09#Orig.EpGreg.7.s26",
    "work_id": "anf-works/origen-letter-to-gregory-anf09",
    "canonical_ref": "Orig.EpGreg.7.s26",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Some of these images, then, are close to the borders of the heathen, which the brothers, as we showed, of Ader have devised.",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 238,
    "date_range": [
